/K [0]
>>
endobj
178 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 139 0 R
/E (Criminology education demands practical competencies, especially in technical subjects like Forensic Ballistics. While Competency-Based Learning \(CBL\) connects instruction with professional expectations, students still face challenges in course content, laboratory resources, activities, and instructional support. Despite existing local studies, there is a lack of institution-specific data at PHILCST. Thus, this descriptive-quantitative study aims to identify the learning challenges of fourth-year Criminology students in Forensic Ballistics \(A.Y. 2026-2027\) across four key dimensions to develop an evidence-based Learning Enhancement Plan.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
